cit scope-gated EVE send and exact XYZ range intersection","Manual Ansiblex add/toggle/delete and CSV bridge-list import/toggle/delete","Unchanged user SMT list imports eleven reciprocal pairs and round-trips all twenty-two unknown-ID directions","Pinned portal map 390","Thera and Turnur entrances are visible and explorable on the map with attributed hover details and honest stale/expired states","Pinned map explanations support keyboard dismissal, mobile layout and entrance route drafts without changing saved itineraries","Pilot and fleet symbols explain their meaning through actual map mouseover and dismiss pinned details when their layer is hidden","Operational notebook 390","Private intel, alert acknowledgement, expired history, authorized pilots/fleet and source-aware public observations","Scanner review/import, partial-versus-complete scans, private infrastructure and responsive notebook","Physical, schematic and exact two-hop local radar projections retain honest distance semantics","Private tactical popup keeps the same map/camera, receives hidden-parent SSE updates and restores without claiming always-on-top","Discovered J-space bounded minimum zoom","Map-owned wormhole confirmation, lifetime editing, immediate expiry removal and preserved system knowledge","J-space keeps system search and discovery context while hiding region navigation, grouping and internal geography","J-Space opens a user-map landing, the source is reachable only through settings, and every creation form collects name, description, pilots and optional scope without a tracking opt-in","The live source is read-only, its creation form builds an independent map with the selected roster, and system/region scope anchors save and clear through visible controls","Map pilots are explicit, default to tracking when added and can be paused, resumed or removed without changing another map","J-Space uses the remaining window height and sidebar collapse returns more than200 pixels to the map","Card movement follows real pointer input within two frames, stays optimistic during a delayed save and persists a second gesture in order","Compact connection workspace 390","Mobile fit keeps visible overview names and connection ports inside the viewport without overlapping neighboring labels","Compact readable cards expose pointer and keyboard ports, preserve the pending visual and create only unconfirmed observations; canceled, self and empty drops leave the map unchanged","Permanent chain search frames existing systems without duplicate writes; one-click status, role and condition changes record lifetime presets and retain unconfirmed route trust","Right-click lifetime and mass changes persist lifetime, mass and ship size with separate line colors; system menus have one System details destination plus distinct map, zKillboard and K-Space actions","Connection deletion forgets canonical edges immediately; system and group Undo restores cards without reviving deleted connections","Alliance and corporation name search show logos, support keyboard selection and fill the correct EVE ID without manual entry","One persistent System/Scanner/Reports/Notes/Navigate/Intel menu keeps the selected system; assigned wormhole ownership appears on its card","J225111 C4/C1/C3 reference cards, symbol explanations, persisted group drag/lock/keyboard layout, undo and reduced-motion pan/zoom","Quick condition updates preserve a confirmed connection’s exact expiry and existing routing permissions","Scanner navigation to a system outside the private chain keeps the requested tool open without adding a map card","A delayed partial-scan preview cannot import after the user leaves the Scanner tool","A card opens the visible J-Space scanner in one click; partial updates preserve absent signatures while complete scans retain explicit missing-signature review","Canonical scanner updates, bookmark text and deletion restore preserve observation age and attach to the exact connection","Two-sided connection conditions use canonical links, explicit route access, unchanged itineraries and an honest passage ledger","Field notes retain trusted pilot attribution, portraits and compact deletion; contextual text/author search can open another system’s notes within the map","Structures and timers have separate forms, lists and map badges; new observation time defaults to current UTC and editing preserves its original timestamp","Reviewed D-scan structure imports, EVE-time timers, expiring local rallies and contextual notes persist without inventing access or power state","Positive structure, timer, signature and note counts fit inside system cards and open their detail tabs; zero-count metrics and redundant connection link icons stay hidden","Wanderer v1 migration preserves positions and context without reviving historical links or overwriting current scans","J-Space chain mobile","Map rename/export/import preserves context with unconfirmed copied links; pilot isolation and workspace restoration work on desktop and mobile","Private lifetime expiry removes its line, closes connection details and forgets data and notes without a refresh, while retaining system cards","Nearest-exit discovery excludes unconfirmed or unsuitable passages, respects vessel limits and copies an evidenced one-jump route without changing EVE navigation","Thera reports show current observation age, expire during repeated workspace refreshes, and support explicit adoption without granting route access","Closing the planner and choosing a different map destination invalidates prior route results and Send actions, including after navigation remount","Region and constellation previews stay provisional, drag and nudge as one group, cancel without writes, then atomically place individual nodes and real internal stargates","Stargates and Ansiblex have distinct permanent visuals and editors without wormhole conditions; keyboard creation from top to bottom tabs preserves both anchors on one continuous curve",